            "text": "9.1 secrecorded demo"
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "links",
    "links": [
      {
        "text": "Explore the virtual assistance repository",
        "url": "https://github.com/RedaKaleem/virtual-assitance"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "CONTEXT AND OUTCOME"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "Replacing a Physical Controller with Hand Movement"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Context"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Driving games normally depend on a keyboard or controller. This project tests whether a webcam and hand tracking can create a more physical steering interaction without additional hardware."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Outcome"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "I built a Python prototype that tracks both wrists, calculates the angle between them, and converts the result into W A S D keyboard input for straight left right and reverse movement."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading2",
    "text": "How the System Works"
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "file": "image2.png"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "Camera frames become hand geometry direction states and keyboard input"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The challenge"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Create a control gesture that feels understandable while avoiding a separate trained gesture model."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The approach"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Treat the line between two wrists as a virtual steering wheel and use its slope to choose direction."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "KEY STAGES"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "From Wrist Coordinates to Game Input"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "1  Detect"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "MediaPipe finds the hand skeleton and exposes wrist coordinates in each frame."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "2  Measure"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The controller calculates a midpoint slope and steering geometry from both wrists."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "3  Classify"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Tilt thresholds distinguish left right and straight states. One detected hand maps to reverse."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "4  Control"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Windows input structures press and release W A S D scan codes for the game."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image3.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Steering geometry"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image4.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Keyboard input implementation"
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "FINAL DESIGN AND IMPACT"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "A Webcam as the Steering Wheel"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "The working demo combines the game view and live hand tracking on one laptop. The user moves both hands as a wheel while the controller sends directional key input in the background."
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image5.jpg"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Muted demo frame"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image6.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Verified control states"
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading2",
    "text": "Impact"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "The prototype demonstrates a low-cost, vision-based control method using only a webcam. It does not yet include measured latency, accuracy, comfort, or cross-platform support."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "LEARNING AND NEXT STEPS"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "What the Prototype Taught Me"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Learning"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "A simple geometric rule can create a convincing interaction quickly, but fixed thresholds may feel unstable across camera positions and body sizes."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Next step"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Calibrate the neutral pose, smooth wrist coordinates, measure input latency, and test longer play sessions for comfort."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  }
]
